.TH TULPAR-WHY 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.7.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-why \- explain why a package is installed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar why
.RI [ options "] " name
.br
.B tulpar W
.RI [ options "] " name
.br
.B tulpar \-W
.RI [ options "] " name
.SH DESCRIPTION
Explains why
.I name
is on the system. A package installed explicitly is reported as such,
together with any packages that also require it. A package installed
as a dependency is reported with the installed packages that require
it and the shortest chain that leads from an explicitly installed
package to it. A dependency that nothing requires any more is reported
as an orphan, as is a dependency that only other unused packages
require; see
.BR tulpar-orphans (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Operate on the database of an alternate root.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print the explanation as a JSON object instead of human-readable text. See
.BR tulpar-json (7).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the package is not installed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-mark (1),
.BR tulpar-orphans (1),
.BR tulpar-json (7)
